# Python Scanner Standards

## Technology

- Python 3.
- Type hints.
- Pydantic for data validation.
- HTTPX for HTTP operations.
- Asyncio where appropriate.
- OWASP ZAP integration.
- Nuclei integration.

## Architecture

Separate responsibilities into:

- core/: shared scanner functionality.
- jobs/: job execution.
- engines/: scanning engine integrations.
- scope/: target authorization and validation.
- normalization/: common vulnerability schema.
- reporting/: scan result preparation.

## Scanner Integration

- Keep each scanning engine independent.
- Define common scanner interfaces.
- Normalize engine-specific output.
- Capture execution errors.
- Implement timeouts.
- Support graceful cancellation.
- Record scan execution metadata.

## Security

- Never execute arbitrary user-supplied commands.
- Avoid shell=True.
- Use subprocess argument arrays.
- Restrict filesystem access.
- Enforce target scope.
- Validate DNS resolution and redirects.
- Apply concurrency and resource limits.

## Testing

- Use pytest.
- Mock external scanner processes.
- Test malformed scanner output.
- Test timeout handling.
- Test authorization boundaries.